# Git Workflow Commands (Voice Triggers)

**Before any playbook below:** run [git-branch-sync-preflight.mdc](git-branch-sync-preflight.mdc) (fetch + behind-main check + feature-marker spot-check). Sync stale branches with `origin/main` before commit/test so merged features do not “disappear.”

**Model:** use Composer 2.5 Fast (`composer-2.5-fast`) for these git voice commands (cost-efficient).

When the user says one of these phrases, follow the matching playbook. Do **not** ask which files to stage unless the command is ambiguous or secrets are present.

| User says | Action |
|---|---|
| **`git commit all`** | Work-loss review gate → discover scopes → branch per scope → commit each → **push all** new/updated task branches → return to `main` → brief report + unmerged branches |
| **`git commit`** | Same as `git commit all`, but **push only if** the user also said push in the same message; otherwise commit locally and list branches/SHAs |
| **`git workflow`** | Read-only audit + optional commit (see Workflow Audit) |

---

## Work-loss review gate (mandatory)

**Full formula:** [work-loss-review-formula.mdc](work-loss-review-formula.mdc) (classify A–E → W1–W5 → recover before re-implement).

Run **before** staging/committing on `git commit` / `git commit all` / push, **and** when the user reports lost / vanished / disappeared work.

### 1. Assess (read-only) — formula W1–W3

In parallel with preflight:

- Open local + remote task branches ahead of / not in `origin/main` (`git branch -a --no-merged origin/main`)
- `git stash list`; open `gh pr list --state open`
- Recent parent `agent-transcripts/` for SUCCESS / branch names / uncommitted paths
- Keyword/`git log --all` match for the missing feature before assuming it was never built
- Spot-check: would checking out the target branch drop files that exist on `origin/main` or on another unmerged SUCCESS branch?

Say: `Phase: work-loss. Checkout: … Class: … Recover: … Action: …`

### 2. Ask Ezequiel (required — do not skip)

> Ezequiel — work-loss review: class `[A–E]`. Unmerged SUCCESS `[branch @ sha]`. Stashes `[n]`. Other-chat SUCCESS `[titles or none]`. For this commit: **separate** from main, **build on** `<existing-branch>`, or **merge-first**? Recover existing commit before new code?

Wait for the answer before creating branches / committing (unless the user already answered in the same message).

### 3. Proceed only after choice

| Choice | Action |
|---|---|
| Separate | Fresh `main` → new `fix/` / `feat/` / … (prior unmerged branches untouched) |
| Build on | Checkout latest related task branch → merge `origin/main` if behind → commit on top |
| Merge first | Help open/merge PR(s), pull `main`, then commit the new work |

Pushed branches are **not** replaced by a new push elsewhere. Only merge (or explicit abandon) retires them. **Pushed ≠ merged** — remind after every push.

