## Conflicts with older rules

- **`git-commit-push-mastery`**: “ask which group” is **waived** when the user says `git commit all` or `git commit` (this file wins).
- **`git-commit-branch-alignment`**: implement-on-main-first still applies **until** commit time; at `git commit all`, create/reuse task branches and return to `main` after push.
- **User `git commit all` rule**: always **push** after `git commit all` (all new/updated task branches, not `main`).

---

## Secrets and junk

Never stage: `.env`, credentials, `node_modules`, duplicate path variants (`extension\` vs `extension/`), local-only SQL unless the user included it in scope.

---

## Quick reference (agent)

```
lost / vanished → work-loss-review-formula (W1–W5) → recover before re-implement
git commit all  → work-loss ask → split scopes → N branches → push each → main → report SHAs + unmerged
git commit      → work-loss ask → same, push only if user said push
git workflow    → audit (git + stashes + branches + transcripts + logs + safe-loop) → recommend next step
safe loop       → SUCCESS → task branch push → merge PR to main → pull main → next work
```
